{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:13.30.120","page_type":"section"},"citation":"13.30.120","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.120","content_hash":"6712438798077a0bf424c6e07e29c837c7a037852a77486d03c765b314af4c30","heading":"Sampling of stormwater runoff by each industry.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.30.120:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.120","text":"The operator shall upon request by the Utilities Director provide a copy of any stormwater sampling and analysis results required to be submitted to the KDHE under the terms of the industrial stormwater permit. Any additional information about each industry’s sampling program shall be submitted to the Utilities Director upon request including, but not limited to:\n(a) Results from the stormwater sampling;\n(b) Maintenance records on stormwater structural controls;\n(c) Information on the status and performance of stormwater structural controls;\n(d) Information on the status and performance of any stormwater nonstructural controls; and\n(e) Copies of all Superfund Amendments and Reauthorization Act Title III Section 313 reports that contain information on ground water and surface water monitoring, chemical release data, and corrective actions required by the Kansas Department of Health and Environment. (Ord. 20089 § 108, 10-17-17.)\nCross References: Utilities Department, TMC 2.20.110 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"e8d73a28-ab0d-515b-a394-55f247b222cc"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.30.120","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.30.120","content_hash":"846107998d23488b5abaf06cf8febc93d38f56d84377db2211b046d49ba82411","heading":null,"ordinal":